20:29.480 --> 20:33.800
As always, Prema is still a thing, even if they don't perform.

20:33.800 --> 20:35.960
So they use quite some rumours.

20:37.000 --> 20:40.040
Of course, we may see Egozi continue on with them.

20:41.080 --> 20:44.440
But there also, we'll get onto his rumours later though,

20:44.440 --> 20:48.280
but there are rumours of him going into IndyNXT,

20:48.280 --> 20:49.880
which could be interesting.

20:50.680 --> 20:53.880
And then, I mean, we have Hector D'Angelo from EC3

20:53.880 --> 20:55.880
also rumoured to go race with Prema.

20:56.520 --> 20:57.800
Dall’Agnol.

20:58.520 --> 21:01.080
Oh my god, I can't say this guy's name right, can I?

21:01.080 --> 21:01.580
It's okay.

21:01.580 --> 21:02.080
I'm sorry.

21:03.160 --> 21:05.720
Hector Dall’Agnol from Palou Motorsports.

21:06.840 --> 21:10.600
And then Perard again, it's basically the Palou Motorsports guys

21:10.600 --> 21:13.000
and then Garfias repeating the year.

21:13.000 --> 21:16.440
I mean, yeah, Prema downfall is real,

21:16.440 --> 21:17.880
when you look at their line-ups.

21:19.160 --> 21:21.480
I feel like at least this year, they still have some,

21:22.280 --> 21:24.840
look at that, they have, they basically have KNB.

21:25.800 --> 21:27.560
And then it's going to get like next year,

21:27.560 --> 21:29.080
they're going to have literally nobody.

21:30.040 --> 21:32.200
It's just a bit depressing to think about,

21:32.200 --> 21:35.560
like three years ago where they were compared to now.

21:37.080 --> 21:38.840
We can't always talk about the same things.

21:38.840 --> 21:41.960
We have to talk about AIX where I read rumours

21:41.960 --> 21:46.680
that Barrichello had signed a one plus one year contract,

21:46.680 --> 21:50.200
which, I mean, I get it, but I also kind of don't

21:51.000 --> 21:55.560
because I do not remember him doing anything really this season.

21:56.280 --> 22:00.200
I mean, the AIX are usually quite in the back.

22:00.200 --> 22:03.560
I think Brad Benavides got us hopeful last year

22:03.560 --> 22:07.160
that maybe they can become, you know, a serious team

22:07.160 --> 22:08.920
and I never know if it's the driver or 

22:08.920 --> 22:10.920
if it's the car that's struggling.

22:10.920 --> 22:13.880
I mean, we will see Brad returning from injury.

22:14.920 --> 22:15.800
He should be back.

22:16.760 --> 22:19.320
Yeah, but I don't know.

22:19.320 --> 22:21.240
Like will he do F3 again?

22:21.240 --> 22:23.560
Have there been rumours that he will do F3 again?

22:24.440 --> 22:26.520
Because even if he finishes this season,

22:27.640 --> 22:30.920
like his career has been so ****

22:30.920 --> 22:33.160
and I'm really sorry for him kind of, but.

22:33.880 --> 22:36.440
But he's raced in F2, maybe he goes back to F2.

22:37.400 --> 22:39.320
I mean, if we see him in F2,

22:39.320 --> 22:41.400
I think it will be quite like the story

22:41.400 --> 22:43.960
that he's managed to, you know, finds a way back.

22:44.920 --> 22:49.880
But I'm just kind of, I never know what's going on at AIX.

22:49.880 --> 22:52.200
Either ways, I don't know if it's a sensible thing

22:52.200 --> 22:54.360
to sign a one plus one year contract

22:54.360 --> 22:57.720
because the idea of signing a contract that ensures

22:57.720 --> 23:00.280
if your first F3 season doesn't go to plan,

23:00.280 --> 23:02.120
you can, you know, return is a good thing.

23:02.680 --> 23:05.720
But do you want to do that with AIX?

23:06.840 --> 23:07.480
Yeah.

23:09.240 --> 23:11.160
Because I feel like,

23:11.480 --> 23:14.440
and like I don't really look out for Barrichello.

23:14.440 --> 23:18.920
I feel like if I were him and this season's ****,

23:18.920 --> 23:20.600
you know, but we also expected that

23:20.600 --> 23:22.040
because he was coming from like,

23:22.040 --> 23:23.480
was it EuroFormula Open?

23:24.040 --> 23:25.640
Yeah, a lot of the,

23:25.640 --> 23:29.080
basically the guys who aren't so good have come from EFO.

23:29.960 --> 23:32.600
Either ways, so you come from EuroFormula Open,

23:32.600 --> 23:34.200
you don't have the same,

23:34.200 --> 23:36.520
like EuroFormula Open also drives some circuits,

23:36.520 --> 23:37.640
but it's a different experience

23:37.640 --> 23:40.920
and if you were to drive FREC, you come there,

23:41.000 --> 23:43.960
you're in a bad team and like,

23:43.960 --> 23:45.560
you know, for the first year,

23:45.560 --> 23:47.800
just gaining experience is probably fine.

23:48.360 --> 23:50.120
But if you really want to perform

23:50.120 --> 23:53.160
and your goal is still to, you know,

23:53.160 --> 23:54.200
really go somewhere,

23:54.200 --> 23:56.520
not just waste money having fun driving,

23:57.480 --> 24:00.280
I would have tried to get a better seat.

24:00.280 --> 24:03.560
You know, I'm not saying like Campos or Trident,

24:03.560 --> 24:05.560
but I'm saying like, you know,

24:05.560 --> 24:07.720
maybe Van Amersfoort, maybe ART,

24:08.600 --> 24:09.720
like those, maybe Rodin,

24:09.720 --> 24:11.160
and like those teams that are not

24:12.040 --> 24:13.720
fighting for the championship,

24:13.720 --> 24:15.880
but you know that they can at least get points.

24:17.400 --> 24:19.240
And I heard that they,

24:20.600 --> 24:22.360
the other AIX guys,

24:22.360 --> 24:23.720
whoever's with them right now,

24:24.280 --> 24:26.920
they're looking to repeat the year.

24:28.280 --> 24:31.240
Yeah, I think moving on to FREC now,

24:31.240 --> 24:33.320
because thinking where things get more interesting,

24:33.320 --> 24:35.320
I feel like there's nothing too

24:36.360 --> 24:38.600
out of the blue in F2 and F3,

24:39.480 --> 24:42.680
but FREC, I mean, I think the big thing is DVL.

24:42.680 --> 24:45.880
I would say there's already been some early testing,

24:45.880 --> 24:47.400
FREC, with a bunch of drivers.

24:48.200 --> 24:49.160
Not just DVL,

24:50.040 --> 24:52.760
but I feel like it's really important to mention that we have,

24:52.760 --> 24:54.920
and I called that last year,

24:54.920 --> 25:00.120
we're going to have like Avengers Endgame of Racing,

25:00.120 --> 25:03.880
because you have all of these incredibly talented,

25:03.880 --> 25:05.480
great drivers coming from F4,

25:05.480 --> 25:09.320
because we had a really, really strong F4 field at the moment.

25:09.320 --> 25:10.920
It has been so spread out.

25:10.920 --> 25:12.280
We've had guys in British,

25:12.840 --> 25:13.560
Italian,

25:14.120 --> 25:18.920
Spanish, all of these guys,

25:18.920 --> 25:20.360
we're going to probably see all the F4,

25:20.360 --> 25:21.880
you know, Spanish F4,

25:22.920 --> 25:23.960
British F4,

25:23.960 --> 25:25.720
and Italian F4 champion,

25:25.720 --> 25:26.920
all fighting each other,

25:26.920 --> 25:27.960
E4 champion.

25:28.680 --> 25:30.360
But also not just the champions,

25:30.360 --> 25:33.080
we also have certain drivers that while

25:33.080 --> 25:37.400
maybe at the moment not quite able to be up to the championship fight,

25:37.400 --> 25:39.960
will be more able to get closer,

25:39.960 --> 25:42.520
and I think will be able to use their experience

25:42.520 --> 25:44.680
and prove themselves further in,

25:45.480 --> 25:46.200
you know, FREC,

25:46.200 --> 25:50.360
because I think we don't just have like one or two drivers

25:50.360 --> 25:51.640
for every championship, we’ll have,

25:51.640 --> 25:53.480
We’ll have a really mixed grid.

25:54.360 --> 25:55.240
I think that's great.

25:56.040 --> 25:58.360
Yeah, the thing with DVL that I find interesting.

25:58.360 --> 26:01.160
Interesting, he's been testing with a bunch of different teams.

26:01.160 --> 26:03.960
Of course, you've had quite a few kind of early tests

26:03.960 --> 26:05.800
where a bunch of drivers have been testing.

26:06.360 --> 26:09.560
But DVL, he's tested with always MP, Rodin,

26:09.560 --> 26:11.640
but no matter what team he's been with,

26:11.640 --> 26:13.000
he's been like the quickest.

26:13.720 --> 26:20.200
I thought that he was like six tenths faster than anyone else.

26:20.200 --> 26:22.360
It was some crazy sh*t like that.

26:23.080 --> 26:24.920
Of course, you know, it's only testing,

26:24.920 --> 26:25.960
yada, yada, yada,

26:25.960 --> 26:29.000
but boy, this is going to be fun to see.

26:29.800 --> 26:32.200
And this R-ace lineup, probably DVL,

26:32.200 --> 26:33.960
and most likely, I mean,

26:33.960 --> 26:35.560
Kenzo’s not tested with them,

26:35.560 --> 26:37.720
but Mercedes, R-ace.

26:37.720 --> 26:41.000
DVL and Kenzo Craigie in the same team is going to be fun.

26:41.640 --> 26:43.240
Oh, I can't wait.

26:44.040 --> 26:45.320
Grids not even confirmed.

26:45.960 --> 26:47.640
And really seeing, I mean,

26:48.280 --> 26:49.960
Kenzo is really coming to his own,

26:49.960 --> 26:51.400
like especially in E4.

26:52.680 --> 26:53.960
He's been doing really well,

26:53.960 --> 26:55.880
and especially in the IF4,

26:55.880 --> 27:01.400
maybe R-ace haven't been up to standards, but.

27:02.040 --> 27:04.920
But they're really more up there in FREC.

27:05.800 --> 27:08.600
I mean, these two guys going against each other

27:08.600 --> 27:10.680
is going to be so much fun.

27:10.680 --> 27:13.560
I think we're going to see rivalries form

27:13.560 --> 27:17.400
that we will generally see all the way through F1.

27:18.120 --> 27:20.360
Like, I really think that we were going to see

27:20.360 --> 27:21.640
some absolute bangers.

27:22.280 --> 27:24.600
They're probably going to see Rocco Coronel,

27:24.760 --> 27:26.440
stepping up from Spanish F4,

27:27.000 --> 27:29.880
who's incredibly exciting as well.

27:29.880 --> 27:31.240
And we did get a preview,

27:31.240 --> 27:33.000
and of course, in the Formula Winter Series.

27:33.720 --> 27:35.880
And of course, [?].

27:36.440 --> 27:38.680
I quite like Scott Lindblom as well.

27:39.480 --> 27:42.280
Okay, maybe he's not as hyped up as the other three,

27:42.280 --> 27:43.400
but I think he's,

27:43.400 --> 27:45.080
I really like his race craft a lot.

27:45.800 --> 27:51.320
I saw tested with both CL and Van Amersfoort,

27:51.320 --> 27:52.840
which made me think that,

27:53.640 --> 27:56.600
and what I expect of a lot more drivers to do like him,

27:57.640 --> 27:59.000
you have certain drivers

27:59.000 --> 28:02.360
who really have a lot more funds like DVL.

28:02.360 --> 28:04.360
I like him, but we cannot ignore that.

28:04.360 --> 28:06.120
He apparently really has the money.

28:06.920 --> 28:08.760
So he has the ability to test.

28:08.760 --> 28:11.160
It's like with Freddie, some drivers,

28:11.160 --> 28:12.520
tjhey’re incredibly talented,

28:12.520 --> 28:15.000
but money goes such a long way.

28:15.000 --> 28:16.520
Yeah, but what I wanted to say about him,

28:16.520 --> 28:20.680
like he's been able to test with like every high team,

28:20.680 --> 28:22.680
and he will be able to choose

28:22.840 --> 28:24.520
which team he likes the best

28:24.520 --> 28:26.840
and which team he feels the most comfortable with

28:26.840 --> 28:29.400
and which team he thinks has the best performance.

28:30.120 --> 28:32.680
Well, you have someone like Lindblom,

28:32.680 --> 28:35.000
who, you know, maybe does not have

28:35.000 --> 28:38.760
just quite as much money and instead has,

28:39.800 --> 28:42.520
it looks to me that his strategy is probably more

28:42.520 --> 28:43.640
with also doing CL,

28:43.640 --> 28:46.840
which is like, you know, rather small team,

28:46.840 --> 28:48.520
like not up in the championship fight.

28:49.000 --> 28:52.040
Um, at least get, you know,

28:52.040 --> 28:53.400
a bit of time in the car

28:53.400 --> 28:55.640
and probably to a lot better price

28:55.640 --> 28:58.200
than what he would get if he were to test with R-ace.

28:59.000 --> 29:01.880
I think one that, or two drivers

29:01.880 --> 29:03.800
that I really think are really interesting

29:03.800 --> 29:05.640
that I am hoping for is,

29:05.640 --> 29:07.240
it's kind of expected

29:07.240 --> 29:10.040
that Alp Aksoy is going to return with Prema.

29:10.920 --> 29:14.280
Um. I remember, I remember the start of the season,

29:14.280 --> 29:16.760
there were rumors of him going straight to F3

29:16.760 --> 29:20.440
because of keeping on the F3 calendar next year.

29:21.000 --> 29:23.800
Yeah, I also thought of that just right now

29:23.800 --> 29:25.320
because he could do both

29:25.320 --> 29:27.880
and I really hope he does FREC instead

29:27.880 --> 29:31.560
because I think going straight to F3

29:31.560 --> 29:34.200
could, you know, potentially ruin his career

29:34.200 --> 29:37.400
and I think he's better off putting himself,

29:37.400 --> 29:41.000
you know, in conversation with, maybe not DVL

29:41.000 --> 29:44.200
because I think we won't see a driver

29:44.200 --> 29:45.640
who has just the money

29:45.640 --> 29:47.320
and the ability,

29:47.320 --> 29:50.360
because I both rate him as a great driver

29:50.360 --> 29:52.280
but also he has the money.

29:52.280 --> 29:56.360
But I think Aksoy is doing himself not a favor

29:56.360 --> 29:58.600
if he tries to go up against drivers

29:58.600 --> 29:59.880
like Wheldon and KNB.

29:59.880 --> 30:03.640
Even, even if he could maybe match them driving wise,

30:04.920 --> 30:07.640
they have years of experience on him

30:07.640 --> 30:11.480
and they have, you know, teams backing them,

30:11.480 --> 30:13.080
huge sponsors.

30:13.080 --> 30:17.880
So I think doing FREC would be the wise choice for him.

30:19.640 --> 30:22.680
Yeah, and like speaking of going F4 to F3,

30:23.400 --> 30:26.600
Fionn McLaughlin, that has not worked out for him at all

30:26.600 --> 30:28.680
and now, like, there are rumors

30:28.680 --> 30:30.360
he's going to be dropped from Red Bull.

30:31.000 --> 30:32.520
We don't even know if he's going to be

30:32.520 --> 30:34.680
fully on the F3 grid next year.

30:35.640 --> 30:37.560
I'll argue for him that, you know,

30:37.560 --> 30:44.360
Italian F4 still is closer to F3 than British F4

30:44.360 --> 30:45.560
is, simply because, you know,

30:47.000 --> 30:49.720
Italian F4 has that mainland Europe.

30:51.080 --> 30:53.080
I don't know, it's hard to explain

30:53.080 --> 30:56.680
but circuits like Monza and Imola

30:56.680 --> 30:58.680
and where, you know, Italian F4 regularly drives,

30:58.680 --> 31:00.600
and they didn't this year,

31:00.600 --> 31:03.480
but they have done before like Red Bull Ring

31:04.120 --> 31:06.200
or, you know, other circuits around.

31:06.920 --> 31:11.400
Spa is closer to what you can expect in F3

31:11.400 --> 31:13.000
than what British F4 does

31:13.000 --> 31:17.880
because British F4 technically only has Silverstone.

31:18.920 --> 31:23.400
And British F4, although I think the top level is great,

31:24.040 --> 31:27.480
it also has a lot of midfield drives

31:27.480 --> 31:30.360
where opposed to that in Italian F4,

31:31.240 --> 31:33.160
you always have incredible drivers.

31:33.160 --> 31:37.640
There's another driver that I care for

31:37.640 --> 31:39.720
that I wanted to bring up with Aksoy

31:39.720 --> 31:42.600
is Ary Bansal who has been testing

31:43.880 --> 31:45.640
sometimes with Trident.

31:45.640 --> 31:48.760
And while I have not heard any, you know,

31:49.880 --> 31:53.320
official things stating that he would do it with Trident,

31:54.280 --> 31:58.840
I would not be surprised if that came out to be true.

31:58.840 --> 32:00.200
You know, it makes sense.

32:01.080 --> 32:06.040
Yeah, of course, I reckon we'll see Bondarev on the grid somewhere.

32:06.760 --> 32:09.560
Of course, there's the news that he's now leaving

32:09.560 --> 32:11.960
Italian F4 for the rest of the season

32:11.960 --> 32:14.760
and he's going to, I think it's CL Motorsport into FREC.

32:15.880 --> 32:19.880
So, I mean, he could really be anywhere on the grid next year.

32:19.880 --> 32:21.160
Just because he's with CL now

32:21.160 --> 32:23.160
doesn't mean he'd be with them next year, but.

32:23.160 --> 32:27.240
I saw someone say that CL is a great move by him

32:27.240 --> 32:30.040
to, you know, learn the vibes and, you know,

32:30.040 --> 32:34.200
he's been struggling in F4 and I think it makes more sense

32:34.200 --> 32:36.840
to, you know, get to know the car a bit

32:36.840 --> 32:41.000
and rather drive from the back than trying to be in the front

32:41.000 --> 32:44.120
and, you know, making everything harder for yourself.

32:44.120 --> 32:48.600
And if you get a few rounds down, you have the vibes of the car.

32:48.600 --> 32:50.360
Since apparently that's not something

32:50.360 --> 32:52.600
that has worked out with him so far.

32:53.320 --> 32:55.880
Then next year, once he has a bit of experience,

32:56.440 --> 33:02.040
going to a better team, but also I'm worrying

33:02.040 --> 33:04.280
how much money he even, you know, has.

33:04.280 --> 33:09.000
And I've seen people bring up that we don't know how serious

33:09.000 --> 33:12.520
Williams is still interested in supporting him

33:12.520 --> 33:17.080
when you have someone like KNB who came into the academy after him.

33:18.600 --> 33:20.680
I'm pretty sure, you have to correct me here

33:20.680 --> 33:23.000
but I'm pretty sure started F4 after him.

33:23.960 --> 33:27.320
Um, KNB started the year before.

33:27.320 --> 33:28.760
Did he?

33:28.760 --> 33:29.160
Yeah.

33:29.160 --> 33:32.040
Yeah, KNB’s first year was 2024.

33:32.920 --> 33:34.040
First full year.

33:34.040 --> 33:36.280
Bondarev did a few races to the end of 2024.

33:36.920 --> 33:40.040
Then Kean got dropped by Alpine.

33:40.920 --> 33:44.280
Then 2025, they're both in IF4.

33:44.280 --> 33:45.320
Then it started this year.

33:45.880 --> 33:49.000
Kean goes up to FREC and joins Williams this year,

33:49.000 --> 33:50.040
I think it was.

33:50.040 --> 33:52.520
Yeah, so thank you for this correction

33:52.520 --> 33:56.440
because I just remembered both of them being there for 24

33:56.440 --> 33:58.600
and I was not sure about 23.

33:58.600 --> 34:03.880
Either way, in any way, the fact that Kean will be in F3

34:04.600 --> 34:09.000
while Bondarev will only have to try to get even anywhere in

34:09.000 --> 34:11.960
FREC, does not seem good for, you know, him.

34:11.960 --> 34:15.560
And I'm pretty sure that Williams doesn't,

34:15.560 --> 34:20.600
don't they have like 10-year-olds in their karting team lining up?

34:21.400 --> 34:27.320
Oh, they have Hoogendoorn, which has been very strong in USF.

34:28.280 --> 34:31.640
So yeah, and then Palacio and Green who are going up to OK.

34:32.440 --> 34:36.760
Yeah, and we're going to probably see Hoogendoorn in F4 somewhere next year.

34:36.760 --> 34:39.320
He's only doing USF as he's not 15 yet.

34:39.960 --> 34:42.200
Yeah, that's kind of the point where I'm thinking, you know,

34:42.200 --> 34:47.320
maybe they decide that, you know, supporting Bondarev is not the way anymore.

34:47.960 --> 34:54.360
Either way, I saw Bearman tested with Van Amersfoort

34:54.360 --> 34:57.320
and I expect him to move up.

34:57.960 --> 35:03.800
Even, you know, if, I don't know, he's not the most interesting driver to me.

35:03.800 --> 35:07.240
I think he's just kind of there, but he definitely has the money for it.

35:08.200 --> 35:12.120
And weirdly enough, Van Amersfoort was also,

35:12.120 --> 35:16.520
from what I remember, a team that had his brother raced with before.

35:16.520 --> 35:22.920
So I guess- Ollie won, he won Italian F4 with Van Amersfoort.

35:24.280 --> 35:27.800
Yeah, I think, you know, that's just how it goes sometimes.

35:28.920 --> 35:31.960
One team that's interesting to me, and that's specifically me,

35:32.520 --> 35:36.040
is obviously the woman involvement at Rodin.

35:36.040 --> 35:39.560
Rodin has been testing with Abbi Pulling,

35:40.120 --> 35:44.120
who I would love to see race in, because she's been in GB3.

35:44.120 --> 35:48.520
But the thing in GB3 is she's been very unlucky for really sh*tty reasons.

35:48.520 --> 35:53.800
Like, was there a chassis crack last year or some sh*t like that?

35:55.240 --> 35:56.680
Either way, she was unlucky.

35:57.400 --> 36:01.640
GB3, again, the top, I really rate some of the drivers

36:01.640 --> 36:05.240
and like the top five drivers of GB3.

36:05.960 --> 36:13.800
But we've seen it with Louis Sharp, who went from GB3 to F3,

36:13.800 --> 36:15.800
and really struggled in his first year.

36:15.800 --> 36:21.960
And I think that's what, was Ninovic, who went to FREC after GB3,

36:21.960 --> 36:26.600
now, you know, seems more prepared for F3 next year?

36:27.640 --> 36:30.040
Yes, yeah, he did GB3 last year.

36:30.680 --> 36:34.040
Yeah, and he's in FREC, and he's, you know, doing very well,

36:34.040 --> 36:35.960
because he had experience in faster cars.

36:36.760 --> 36:41.720
But, you know, maybe lacking a bit of experience on European circuits.

36:41.720 --> 36:44.440
Either way, Abbi Pulling is a driver.

36:44.440 --> 36:47.480
I would also just love to see a bit of female involvement again.

36:48.680 --> 36:54.600
You know, and much more importantly, and what everyone should expect from me is

36:55.160 --> 36:59.160
Rodin has also been testing with Alisha Palmowski.

36:59.160 --> 37:03.640
And I've been told by someone who I trust as a source,

37:03.640 --> 37:10.680
that currently there are no real, you know, discussions for race going on,

37:10.680 --> 37:12.200
because FREC is really expensive.

37:12.200 --> 37:17.000
And if you know Alisha Palmowski, she is very unlucky with sponsors.

37:17.000 --> 37:21.080
Like, she does not have millions to blow every single year.

37:22.120 --> 37:27.000
And sometimes there is no, you know, current discussion.

37:27.000 --> 37:32.680
It could become a thing later on when it's about the F1 Academy sponsoring a seat.

37:32.680 --> 37:35.400
I would absolutely love that.

37:35.400 --> 37:38.360
And I think it would be the greatest thing in the world.

37:38.360 --> 37:39.880
They need to bring that back.

37:39.880 --> 37:41.400
I think I have it in my heart.

37:41.400 --> 37:46.680
They will, because, you know, last year was a bit weird with, you know,

37:46.680 --> 37:49.880
Doriane Pin winning, but, you know, not really wanting,

37:50.440 --> 37:53.160
and not really having a worth in continuing single seaters.

37:53.880 --> 37:55.080
All that drama.

37:55.080 --> 37:59.640
I think this year we have a group of, you know, the leading drivers.

37:59.640 --> 38:05.880
I also expect to see Emma Felbermayr and Nina Gademan in a seat,

38:05.880 --> 38:08.200
not in FREC, but potentially in GB3.

38:08.760 --> 38:11.960
Nina Gademan has recently mentioned in an interview,

38:11.960 --> 38:14.920
being interested in doing Eurocup 3 with MP.

38:14.920 --> 38:16.440
I could see that happening.

38:17.400 --> 38:21.880
And for Palmowski, what's important for me is that she's been doing it with Rodin,

38:21.880 --> 38:25.400
which I think is really good because it means to me that there is

38:25.400 --> 38:28.280
some sort of conversation between her and the team.

38:28.280 --> 38:31.960
And even if it's not FREC, I would really hope for like GB3

38:32.520 --> 38:35.720
or anything in like that range of things.

38:36.600 --> 38:37.880
Yeah, I really do-

38:37.880 --> 38:41.400
I mean, she should step up and they should bring the prize back.

38:42.200 --> 38:45.320
She deserves to step up and alongside them.

38:46.120 --> 38:48.440
But imagine getting two women in the same team.

38:49.000 --> 38:50.440
I think it would be great.

38:50.440 --> 38:53.240
You're going to become the biggest Rodin fan then next year.

38:53.240 --> 38:53.880
I'm going to.

38:53.880 --> 38:54.600
I'm going to.

38:54.600 --> 38:58.600
Like Rodin is New Zealand-ish, no?

38:58.600 --> 39:01.000
I'm going to buy like really big New Zealand flag.

39:01.000 --> 39:07.400
If a woman goes to FREC, I'm going to try to do multiple FREC rounds.

39:07.400 --> 39:08.440
I'm going to call it now.

39:09.080 --> 39:11.400
I mean, they're probably going to be in Hockenheim.

39:12.040 --> 39:14.600
Like in Hockenheim, they'll probably be in Spa again.

39:15.480 --> 39:16.520
Zandvoort.

39:16.520 --> 39:17.400
Are they doing Zandvoort?

39:17.400 --> 39:19.160
Because I would try to do Zandvoort also.

39:20.840 --> 39:21.960
And Red Bull Ring.

39:21.960 --> 39:25.160
That's like the four circuits that I would love to do.

39:25.160 --> 39:27.640
And I could realistically do.

39:27.640 --> 39:30.440
Yeah, Alex's FR tour.

39:31.880 --> 39:33.480
Alex's FREC tour.

39:33.480 --> 39:35.480
Okay, either way.

39:37.240 --> 39:41.000
We also had Lennon testing with Rodin again.

39:41.880 --> 39:44.920
That Rodin family stuff is strong, you know.

39:45.560 --> 39:48.680
I think, I mean, DVL tested with them as well.

39:48.680 --> 39:50.680
I think the only reason he'll go to R-ace,

39:50.680 --> 39:51.640
and not Rodin-

39:51.640 --> 39:55.080
DVL has been generally testing with every f*cking single team

39:55.080 --> 39:57.240
to decide which one is best for him.

39:57.240 --> 39:58.360
It's a bit creepy.

39:58.360 --> 40:01.160
Yeah, which is probably why R-ace makes the most sense.

40:01.960 --> 40:03.720
He's just spying on them in the night.

40:03.720 --> 40:06.360
He's just laying there in the factory spying.

40:06.360 --> 40:10.200
No, it's like, you know, when, you know, like,

40:11.480 --> 40:14.840
these really super rich people can just do whatever.

40:16.200 --> 40:17.720
That's kind of creepy to me, honestly.

40:18.360 --> 40:19.960
Anyways, anyways, anyways.

40:19.960 --> 40:22.520
Going on to other series, as we mentioned earlier.

40:23.240 --> 40:26.680
James Egozi is rumored for IndyNXT.

40:26.680 --> 40:29.480
Which, I mean, we've seen, we saw-

40:29.480 --> 40:31.080
Wait a second, I just remembered something.

40:31.880 --> 40:32.840
We need to go back.

40:32.840 --> 40:33.640
Oh my God.

40:33.640 --> 40:35.240
I know I missed something.

40:35.240 --> 40:39.240
And that is that some driver from Brazilian F4

40:39.240 --> 40:43.640
has mentioned on the stream that he has signed a contract race

40:43.640 --> 40:47.480
in F4 next, not F4, in F3 next year.

40:48.040 --> 40:48.760
That's important.

40:49.720 --> 40:50.920
Needed to mention that one.

40:50.920 --> 40:52.600
Needed to get this one off my chest.

40:52.600 --> 40:53.640
I just remembered.

40:53.640 --> 40:56.600
This is probably going to be an AIX driver.

40:56.600 --> 40:58.760
Oh, that would make sense.

40:58.760 --> 40:59.640
Yeah, probably.

40:59.640 --> 41:01.880
But like, it's important for me to mention it.

41:03.000 --> 41:06.280
I should probably research who it was, but I'm too lazy.

41:06.280 --> 41:10.680
So if you see a Brazilian driver coming straight from F4,

41:10.680 --> 41:12.040
I knew it, I knew it.

41:12.040 --> 41:13.400
You heard it here first.

41:13.400 --> 41:17.160
It's also inviting listeners to do their own research.

41:18.440 --> 41:19.240
Anyways.

41:19.320 --> 41:22.120
Egozi rumored for IndyNXT.

41:22.120 --> 41:26.440
I mean, I could honestly see this working quite well for him,

41:26.440 --> 41:27.160
Cause of course,

41:27.960 --> 41:31.000
We have the Polish guy, Tymek.

41:31.960 --> 41:32.840
The Polish guy.

41:32.840 --> 41:33.640
Kucharczyk.

41:33.640 --> 41:35.480
He's the one I'm talking about.

41:35.480 --> 41:36.040
Yeah, him.

41:36.600 --> 41:39.160
He's in IndyNXT and he's doing quite well.

41:40.600 --> 41:44.200
And he came from like EFO or something.

41:44.760 --> 41:47.000
And Egozi is an EC3 championship-

41:47.960 --> 41:51.320
he's the EC3 championship leader.

41:51.320 --> 41:52.440
He's going to win the championship.

41:53.480 --> 41:56.200
It's inevitable he's going to win it.

41:57.320 --> 41:59.960
I feel like we could see him do quite well.

41:59.960 --> 42:04.600
And of course, being an American, maybe he's targeting IndyCar.

42:04.600 --> 42:07.320
So I feel like that would really make quite a bit of sense.

42:07.320 --> 42:10.040
Isn't he also Spanish or something like that?

42:10.040 --> 42:11.960
He races under the American flag.

42:12.840 --> 42:13.400
Oh.

42:13.400 --> 42:14.440
He races for-.

42:14.440 --> 42:16.520
He races with Palou Motorsport.

42:16.600 --> 42:24.920
No, I was just vibing with the idea of someone racing us with Palou Motorsport and maybe

42:24.920 --> 42:32.520
even getting the attention in Spain by Spanish supporters who also like Palou and kind of

42:32.520 --> 42:35.240
stepping into his footsteps and all of that stuff.

42:35.240 --> 42:35.960
He's American.

42:35.960 --> 42:37.560
He's born in Florida.

42:37.560 --> 42:39.880
Also, just look up his Wikipedia.

42:39.880 --> 42:41.400
Look at his Wikipedia.

42:41.400 --> 42:42.760
He has a really...

42:42.760 --> 42:45.320
This guy has an interesting Wikipedia photo.

42:46.920 --> 42:47.560
Look it up.

42:48.840 --> 42:51.400
To be fair, his first name is Luis.

42:52.040 --> 42:53.640
Like L-U-I-S.

42:53.640 --> 42:54.760
James is his middle name.

42:54.760 --> 42:56.120
I thought it was James.

42:56.120 --> 42:56.840
Oh my God.

42:56.840 --> 42:57.720
Yeah.

42:57.720 --> 42:58.200
Oh God.

42:58.200 --> 42:59.240
We've been living a lie.

43:00.360 --> 43:02.760
What is that Wikipedia picture?

43:03.640 --> 43:03.800
What?

43:03.800 --> 43:05.160
He's straight up sharking it.

43:06.760 --> 43:07.960
Okay, that's insane.

43:09.400 --> 43:12.680
I wonder, where did this photo come from?

43:12.680 --> 43:14.120
His Instagram story.

43:14.120 --> 43:15.720
How does that happen?

43:15.720 --> 43:16.200
Find it.

43:17.000 --> 43:19.800
Either way, he's spiritually Spanish to me.

43:21.320 --> 43:24.040
Maybe it's just because he's been racing so much in Spain

43:24.040 --> 43:26.600
that I automatically just think of him as Spanish.

43:27.160 --> 43:29.480
Yeah, unfortunately, we don't have any photos in this,

43:29.480 --> 43:32.930
but if you are listening, do look up James Egozi’s Wikipedia.

43:33.480 --> 43:34.200
That's beautiful.

43:34.200 --> 43:35.400
Go be amused.

43:36.360 --> 43:39.080
Especially if you're having a bad day, please go find it.

43:39.640 --> 43:41.640
Either way, that's enough.

43:42.280 --> 43:42.920
That's enough.

43:43.560 --> 43:45.320
Now looking towards F4.

43:46.200 --> 43:48.040
Noah Baglin is going to be stuff.

43:48.040 --> 43:50.280
He's confirmed he'll be doing F4 next year.

43:50.920 --> 43:51.960
I think it's Italian F4.

43:51.960 --> 43:53.400
We just don't know with what team.

43:53.400 --> 43:57.080
I mean, maybe Prema given FDA, but...

43:57.080 --> 44:00.760
But I thought Ferrari hated Prema now.

44:00.760 --> 44:03.240
But Maccagnani is Ferrari.

44:03.880 --> 44:05.080
Yeah, I just wanted to say,

44:05.080 --> 44:08.680
it's like another guy who's now again with Prema.

44:09.240 --> 44:14.040
I think Prema is still pretty strong in Italian F4.

44:14.040 --> 44:20.440
So, you know what, I think we could also see him

44:20.440 --> 44:23.080
depending on how much money he has, in US Racing

44:23.080 --> 44:26.200
because it's all just pay to win.

44:26.920 --> 44:31.960
Yeah, maybe, I mean, Trident have been looking good here, maybe.

44:32.600 --> 44:34.600
Who knows, you can probably see James and...

44:35.560 --> 44:38.920
That's not how you spell his last name.

44:38.920 --> 44:40.680
It's Anagnostiadis.

44:40.680 --> 44:42.520
Yeah, he'd be with R-ace.

44:42.520 --> 44:45.640
Wait, I need to spell out how it's written here.

44:45.640 --> 44:49.080
It's written as Anagonditadias.

44:49.880 --> 44:50.840
Who wrote that?

44:52.840 --> 44:56.040
That wasn’t me, and I think Robin though.

44:56.040 --> 44:59.560
There's someone who misspelled so many names on here.

44:59.560 --> 45:04.120
Someone also misspelled Rocco Coronel as Rocco Connell.

45:05.000 --> 45:07.720
And I was so confused who you're talking about.

45:08.440 --> 45:11.800
I was worried that this would be very badly done, but it's okay.

45:11.800 --> 45:15.560
But Anagonditadias, that's crazy.

45:17.400 --> 45:22.040
He would be with R-ace, because Mercedes and R-ace are besties now.

45:22.680 --> 45:27.320
But interestingly, the other Ferrari karting driver who's stepping up,

45:27.880 --> 45:31.320
Filippo Sala, he's moving to Spanish F4.

45:32.040 --> 45:33.480
How is that allowed? Wow.

45:34.120 --> 45:35.800
Yeah, Spanish F4.

45:36.600 --> 45:38.120
What even happens in Spanish-

45:38.120 --> 45:42.760
Like, genuinely, one of the biggest points of criticism that I've seen

45:42.760 --> 45:47.720
and that I've heard of drivers is that since Spanish F4 drives without good tires,

45:47.720 --> 45:51.960
it makes it harder to do like...

45:51.960 --> 45:55.720
I heard it from Emma Felbermayr who complained because in F1 Academy

45:55.720 --> 45:59.000
and in British F4, they're driving Pirelli tires,

45:59.000 --> 46:02.120
which feel very different to what she drove in Spanish F4,

46:02.120 --> 46:05.720
which is why she decided to not do Spanish F4 again,

46:05.720 --> 46:08.360
because she felt like it was so stupid.

46:08.360 --> 46:16.760
And I'm just wondering why he would go to Spanish F4 then,

46:16.760 --> 46:19.320
especially if you're a Ferrari Academy member.

46:19.320 --> 46:20.360
He's also Italian.

46:21.320 --> 46:24.440
Why are you? I just thought maybe he's Spanish

46:24.440 --> 46:28.760
and that's why he's wanting to stay in his glorious homeland.

46:28.760 --> 46:31.800
No, what? Why is he going to Spain?

46:32.120 --> 46:34.040
He's Ferrari and he's Italian.

46:34.040 --> 46:37.480
You would expect him to continue on into Italian F4.

46:37.480 --> 46:40.680
All I can think of is probably just funding.

46:42.200 --> 46:48.040
I mean, alright, you know, maybe, maybe Ferrari doesn't give any money at all,

46:48.040 --> 46:51.880
but just like Spanish F4, man.

46:53.080 --> 46:56.440
Or what I could imagine is if you know,

46:56.440 --> 47:00.440
like Noah Baglin is, you know, doing Italian F4 already

47:00.440 --> 47:05.240
and maybe Ferrari wants to split it up

47:05.240 --> 47:10.440
like the way we've had it split up with all the good drivers in F4 this year,

47:10.440 --> 47:12.120
where they're all in different things.

47:12.120 --> 47:14.440
So they can, you know, do their own thing

47:14.440 --> 47:20.280
and not have that huge rivalry from their first ever race on,

47:20.840 --> 47:23.560
which would obviously impact how they drive each other.

47:24.360 --> 47:27.560
And like both of them drive for their own title.

47:27.560 --> 47:31.080
And if they have like a bit of confidence, a bit of experience,

47:31.080 --> 47:32.520
also their own sponsors,

47:33.240 --> 47:39.400
put them together in FREC, or you separate them for longer.

47:40.120 --> 47:42.600
And you can also make the decision better

47:42.600 --> 47:45.560
than whom of the two you want to support long term

47:45.560 --> 47:48.440
because Ferrari supporting two guys,

47:48.440 --> 47:52.280
that are basically in the same championship

47:52.280 --> 47:56.120
is not something that we see often of them.

47:57.080 --> 48:00.280
Yeah, a little thing now, the F1 Academy.

48:00.280 --> 48:02.600
I want to say F1 Academy, can I say F1 Academy?

48:02.600 --> 48:03.800
Of course, I can leave it to you.

48:03.800 --> 48:04.760
Of course.

48:04.760 --> 48:05.320
Thank you.

48:06.040 --> 48:09.160
Okay, so we need to go in because there's a lot of things.

48:09.800 --> 48:12.280
Not a lot of things we expect, a lot of things are rumored.

48:13.560 --> 48:17.800
Most notably rumored, and this one's really just a rumor,

48:17.800 --> 48:19.240
but everyone expects it so heavily,

48:19.240 --> 48:21.160
I'm really going to be surprised if it doesn't happen,

48:21.160 --> 48:23.320
is that Larson returns with Ferrari.

48:23.960 --> 48:25.560
If you are confused now

48:25.560 --> 48:28.120
because F1 Academy has a two year limit,

48:29.000 --> 48:32.600
yeah, kind of, no, because last year they announced

48:32.600 --> 48:35.960
that if everyone felt it was appropriate,

48:35.960 --> 48:38.040
a driver could do a third season.

48:38.040 --> 48:40.120
That's generally something that a lot of drivers

48:40.120 --> 48:43.000
who are in their second season now, including Nina Gademan,

48:43.000 --> 48:46.040
or Emma Felbermayr I have talked kind of about

48:46.040 --> 48:48.760
in the way it's like, no, they're not even considering it,

48:48.760 --> 48:51.080
which I think is a good thing.

48:51.080 --> 48:54.360
The thing is, Alba Larson is currently like ninth

48:54.360 --> 48:55.640
in the championship.

48:55.640 --> 48:57.400
She's in the middle of her second season.

48:57.400 --> 49:00.760
She has not had a single podium in F1 Academy.

49:01.320 --> 49:04.040
I mean, she did one in British F4,

49:04.040 --> 49:08.360
but since she is becoming more and more kind of the face

49:08.360 --> 49:11.320
of F1 Academy, if you ask someone

49:11.320 --> 49:13.480
who does not watch F1 Academy to name a driver,

49:13.480 --> 49:15.880
everyone's going to name her because she's popular.

49:15.880 --> 49:17.480
She's the Instagram follower.

49:17.480 --> 49:18.520
She's always doing something.

49:18.520 --> 49:22.760
There are many people who expect Ferrari

49:22.760 --> 49:25.320
to not care about her driving,

49:25.320 --> 49:30.040
and instead just care about not having to give a big f*ck

49:30.040 --> 49:31.960
about who they would support.

49:31.960 --> 49:33.960
So it's expected she will return.

49:35.640 --> 49:39.720
Another one which is heavily expected or almost announced

49:39.720 --> 49:45.560
is Ginevra Panzeri, who has scored the VCARB support

49:45.560 --> 49:46.440
with Campos.

49:46.920 --> 49:51.000
Ginevra Panzeri has been driving like every single F4 series this year.

49:51.000 --> 49:54.600
She's been in French F4, Central European Zone F4,

49:54.600 --> 49:56.040
I think even Italian F4.

49:56.040 --> 49:57.080
She's been everywhere.

49:59.880 --> 50:03.960
I think the main reason where this came up was in French F4

50:03.960 --> 50:06.440
where one weekend she had a really good one

50:06.440 --> 50:09.560
and she was like P7 and P6.

50:09.560 --> 50:11.240
And it was really rainy.

50:11.560 --> 50:16.760
It was really rainy and there were multiple rumors

50:16.760 --> 50:18.680
of also Alpine looking at her.

50:18.680 --> 50:20.840
But from everything we heard so far,

50:20.840 --> 50:23.960
it's pretty certain that VCARB locked her down,

50:23.960 --> 50:28.120
which with Campos, if we see their performance this year,

50:28.120 --> 50:29.160
is a good choice.

50:30.040 --> 50:32.680
It's genuinely expected that most drivers

50:32.680 --> 50:35.880
in like their first year, including like Matilda Paatz

50:35.880 --> 50:40.600
Lisa Billard, Megan Bruce, that they’ll all return.

50:40.680 --> 50:44.520
It's kind of a bit more of a difficult thing,

50:44.520 --> 50:47.640
but I don't want to go into detail about every single driver.

50:48.360 --> 50:53.320
It's just like most drivers just do a second season.

50:53.320 --> 50:54.760
For most of them, it makes sense.

50:56.040 --> 50:59.720
We also expect to see the wildcards return,

50:59.720 --> 51:04.920
except for Shi Wei because no one knows who Shi Wei even is.

51:07.320 --> 51:08.760
Not as a reason no one knows.

51:08.760 --> 51:10.680
It's the fact that we still don't know her age,

51:10.680 --> 51:11.480
which is kind of weird.

51:12.040 --> 51:15.080
But it's really expected that Chiara Bättig

51:15.640 --> 51:18.680
will be with Red Bull, with Campos,

51:18.680 --> 51:20.120
and fight for the championship.

51:21.960 --> 51:26.200
There is a big chance that Luna Fluxa

51:26.200 --> 51:28.120
will be a wildcard later this season.

51:28.120 --> 51:30.920
I think Las Vegas was what people assumed.

51:30.920 --> 51:33.880
And that she would go on to maybe come in

51:33.880 --> 51:36.280
because she's a Mercedes junior.

51:37.160 --> 51:40.440
We have Peyton Westcott currently as Mercedes junior,

51:40.440 --> 51:42.040
so we're going to see.

51:44.360 --> 51:46.840
But it will also be interesting because...

51:46.840 --> 51:53.000
Oh, Ella Hakkinen will turn 16 as far as I know in December.

51:53.000 --> 51:56.360
So there's a big chance that we will also see her

51:56.360 --> 51:59.000
take over Ella Lloyd's McLaren seat.

51:59.720 --> 52:01.960
Other than that, it's still kind of unsure

52:02.760 --> 52:06.600
whom of the wildcards and whom of other drivers coming in.

52:06.600 --> 52:11.880
Like Jordyn Martin, who's currently the best female in GB4,

52:11.880 --> 52:14.600
which gives you a certain sponsorship

52:14.600 --> 52:17.080
of like 50,000 pounds or something like that.

52:19.480 --> 52:22.280
We have a handful of drivers who we expect to see.

52:22.280 --> 52:24.200
And of those handful of drivers we expect to see,

52:24.840 --> 52:26.600
it's still kind of unclear where...

52:27.000 --> 52:30.600
What's the word… sponsors for?

52:30.600 --> 52:34.440
Like Alpine will be free again.

52:34.440 --> 52:38.760
We have a few brands who will be free to support someone else again.

52:39.720 --> 52:43.640
I think that's something that we will discuss in a few months again, maybe.

52:44.360 --> 52:46.680
Yeah, I think that's all that I have to say about women.

52:47.640 --> 52:52.680
Alba Larson doing another third year would be incredibly interesting.

52:53.480 --> 52:57.240
I mean, I don't think she's got any podiums or anything.

52:58.760 --> 53:01.560
It's just a marketing thing it honestly feels like.

53:03.160 --> 53:05.880
I'm just sorry for her and I always say it like that because,

53:07.160 --> 53:12.120
I feel like she's been done wrong by so many people around her because

53:13.000 --> 53:16.920
every single time that I see other drivers like testing cars,

53:17.480 --> 53:21.240
going to other championships, the only thing that I really see of her

53:21.240 --> 53:25.400
is that either she's part of some fashion campaign

53:26.040 --> 53:32.520
or that she's doing some, you know, out of the car thing for women.

53:32.520 --> 53:37.080
I know she's recently had this karting event with a lot of girls

53:37.080 --> 53:44.200
and support girls get their first kart raced, which is a great thing for her.

53:44.200 --> 53:47.960
And I'm pretty sure that's a great thing for the woman involved.

53:47.960 --> 53:51.640
But the thing is, her own career just seems to be

53:52.440 --> 54:02.040
like the last thought anyone has really in mind because I know she also does one-off races.

54:02.040 --> 54:08.680
She did some one-off races like two or three in British F4 and I was at Zandvoort.

54:08.680 --> 54:10.600
I like seeing her there.

54:10.600 --> 54:14.680
I just wish that she did majority of that season the way that like

54:15.160 --> 54:21.880
Emma Felbermayr is doing one-off entries in British F4, but she’s also doing multiple races in Italian F4.

54:24.200 --> 54:27.320
There's other drivers, even if they're not racing, like Nina Gademan,

54:27.320 --> 54:31.560
who was mentioned testing EC3 cars with MP before.

54:32.200 --> 54:35.720
Those so many things really matter and that's also things that I think

54:35.720 --> 54:41.480
will keep her even after her third season from in any way improving on her abilities

54:41.480 --> 54:43.160
and gaining another seat.

54:45.080 --> 54:48.600
I feel like beyond that, I don't have too much else to say.

54:48.600 --> 54:54.920
I mean, although in EC3, Gino Trappa has said he's competing in another year of EC3.

54:56.120 --> 55:01.320
Aside from that, because in F4 we normally find out incredibly late.

55:02.760 --> 55:08.600
I mean, F4 always kind of depends on how the season went for the drivers themselves

55:08.600 --> 55:12.760
and then you also have karting drivers and for them it's...

55:13.720 --> 55:16.920
I mean, F4 depending on the championship can be super expensive,

55:16.920 --> 55:24.120
but sometimes these kids have very little sponsors and it's all really dramatic.

55:24.840 --> 55:26.040
So we're going to see.

55:27.320 --> 55:34.760
I hope that we manage to do another episode later in the season

55:34.760 --> 55:36.840
where we can maybe discuss a few of these things,

55:37.480 --> 55:42.760
look back on the rumors, discuss the upcoming grids.

55:44.040 --> 55:45.080
But I think other than that.

55:47.000 --> 55:49.080
I think that is all for this week.

55:50.600 --> 55:53.960
Join us next time as we will discuss

55:53.960 --> 55:56.360
British F4 finally returning to racing.

55:56.360 --> 56:03.960
With summer break over, with British F4 and F1 Academy returning this upcoming weekend.

56:04.760 --> 56:09.960
So join us then and as always, let us know your thoughts and comments.

56:09.960 --> 56:11.480
We love hearing from you guys.

56:13.240 --> 56:14.520
And yeah. Thank you for listening.


